************** G E N E R A L   I N F O R M A T I O N *************4249 1451   26
                                                                  4249 1451   27
This evaluated data file is based on a software system built      4249 1451   28
around the nuclear model code TALYS [kon23], version 2.0. It is   4249 1451   29
part of a large collection of isotopic evaluations, all created by4249 1451   30
running the system with either adjusted or default input          4249 1451   31
parameters. This means that the data in the entire collection have4249 1451   32
been tested in detail for many isotopes against individual        4249 1451   33
experimental data, while for other isotopes it is only as good as 4249 1451   34
the global quality of TALYS at the moment. The mutual quality of  4249 1451   35
all individual data files is however consistent: The same set of  4249 1451   36
nuclear models is used and, equally important, the same ENDF-6    4249 1451   37
formatting procedures for each isotope. The data file has been    4249 1451   38
created automatically using the ENDF-6 format generator TEFAL.    4249 1451   39
                                                                  4249 1451   40
The resulting data file provides a complete representation of     4249 1451   41
nuclear data needed for transport, activation, damage, heating,   4249 1451   42
radioactivity, and shielding applications over the incident       4249 1451   43
neutron energy range from 1.e-11 to 200. MeV.                     4249 1451   44
                                                                  4249 1451   45
All transport and activation data for neutrons, charged particles,4249 1451   46
photons and residual nuclides are filed. This includes cross      4249 1451   47
sections, angular distributions, double-differential spectra,     4249 1451   48
isomeric production, discrete and continuum photon production     4249 1451   49
cross sections, residual production cross sections and recoils.   4249 1451   50
This general purpose evaluation can thus be used as both          4249 1451   51
transport and activation library.                                 4249 1451   52
                                                                  4249 1451   53
A complete set of covariance data is included, which is stored    4249 1451   54
in MF31-40.                                                       4249 1451   55
                                                                  4249 1451   56
