***************************** T A L Y S **************************4249 1451  130
                                                                  4249 1451  131
TALYS is a computer code system for the prediction and analysis   4249 1451  132
of nuclear reactions. TALYS simulates reactions that involve      4249 1451  133
neutrons, gamma-rays, protons, deuterons, tritons, helions and    4249 1451  134
alpha-particles, in the 1 keV - 200 MeV energy range. This is     4249 1451  135
achieved by implementing a suite of nuclear reaction models into  4249 1451  136
a single code system. This nuclear data file is based on a        4249 1451  137
theoretical analysis that utilizes the optical model, compound    4249 1451  138
nucleus statistical theory, fission, direct reactions and         4249 1451  139
pre-equilibrium processes, in combination with databases and      4249 1451  140
models for nuclear structure. The following output of TALYS is    4249 1451  141
stored in this data file:                                         4249 1451  142
                                                                  4249 1451  143
- Total, elastic and non-elastic cross sections                   4249 1451  144
- Inelastic cross sections to discrete states                     4249 1451  145
- Exclusive channel cross sections, e.g. (n,g), (n,2n), (n,np),.. 4249 1451  146
- Inelastic scattering angular distributions to discrete states   4249 1451  147
- Exclusive channel energy spectra                                4249 1451  148
- Exclusive channel double-differential spectra                   4249 1451  149
- Exclusive gamma production for discrete states and continuum    4249 1451  150
- Elastic scattering angular distributions                        4249 1451  151
- Recoil data                                                     4249 1451  152
- Total particle cross sections, e.g. (n,xn), (n,xp),..           4249 1451  153
- Total particle energy spectra                                   4249 1451  154
- Total particle double-differential spectra                      4249 1451  155
- Isomeric and ground state cross sections                        4249 1451  156
- Residual production cross sections                              4249 1451  157
                                                                  4249 1451  158
For a description of the used nuclear models and their            4249 1451  159
parameterization we refer to [kon19]. If for this specific        4249 1451  160
nuclide we deviate from the global parameterization, it is made   4249 1451  161
explicit above under Nuclide Specific Information.                4249 1451  162
                                                                  4249 1451  163
